544, 61.579, 61.626, 61.684, 61.719, 61.788, 61.846, 61.962, 62.044, 62.125, 62.229, 62.38, 62.589, 62.659, 62.717, 62.74, 62.833, 62.891, 63.007, 63.077, 63.123, 63.181, 63.239, 63.309, 63.367, 63.541, 63.657, 63.785, 63.901, 63.983, 64.575, 64.749, 64.807, 64.876, 64.935, 64.981, 65.051, 65.109, 65.167, 65.213, 65.248, 65.271, 65.306, 65.341, 65.387, 65.503, 65.55, 65.921, 66.003, 66.061, 66.107, 66.154, 66.212, 66.27, 66.305, 66.374, 66.432, 66.49, 66.537, 66.618, 66.688, 66.839, 66.908, 67.071, 67.117, 67.524]}, "text": "Odysseus finds the giant's own club, an olive trunk as big as a ship's mast. He cuts off a length, sharpens it, and hardens the point in the fire.\n\n\"Who helps me carry the stake? Draw lots,\" said Odysseus.\n\n\"And if he wakes up?\" a crewman asked.\n\n\"Then it was a short plan.\"\n\nHe hides the stake under dung, the one thing a cave full of sheep has plenty of.\n\nThat evening, two more. Six men gone.\n\n\"You have eaten a great deal of man's flesh, Cyclops. Have some wine,\" said Odysseus, quite calmly.\n\nThe wine comes from a priest of Apollo, whose household drank it mixed twenty parts water to one. The giant drinks three bowls. Homer counts.\n\n\"More. Now tell me your name, and I will give you a present,\" the giant rumbled.\n\n\"My name is Nobody,\" said Odysseus.\n\n\"Nobody. Then here is my present, Nobody. I will eat Nobody's friends first, and Nobody last.\"\n\n\"I am honoured.\"\n\nIt does buy time."}